msgstr "This is the <0>master switch + source configuration</0> for web search. Only once it's on can each <1>Agent's configuration</1> individually choose whether to enable <2>web_search</2> (which returns only titles/links/snippets, not the body; fetching the body is WebFetch's job). Web search <3>does not</3> go through the recording proxy and is independent of traffic capture.<4/>Sources: <5>DuckDuckGo (ddgs)</5> (no key needed), <6>Brave (free tier)</6> (needs a Brave API key), <7>Tavily</7> (needs a Tavily API key), or <8>DeepSeek</8> (reuses the current LLM profile). When the master switch is off, each Agent's web-search toggle is unavailable."

